    "apply_transfers": {
      "source_index": 8,
      "index": 8,
      "doc": " Apply a batch of transfers in the given (canonical) order, atomically. Any conservation\n violation `abort`s the whole transaction → every prior mutation in this call rolls back,\n which is exactly the TS RESOURCE PHASE's \"reject the whole action, leave state untouched\".\n\n The off-chain SDK is responsible for ordering `transfers` canonically (by actor, index);\n the chain replays that order faithfully and re-validates conservation — it never trusts\n the off-chain computation, it re-checks it. This is the trustless guarantee.\n\n Gated by StorytellerCap so only the saga's director can settle a resolved event's\n resource outcomes (called from `event::resolve_event` in DR-2).",
      "attributes": [],
      "visibility": "Public",
      "entry": false,
      "type_parameters": [],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "cap",
          "type_": {
            "Reference": [
